{"name":"Polka Dot Skirt","hex":"#fde2a0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"polka","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lively dance originating in Bohemia.","The music for this dance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dance the polka."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polka"},{"term":"dot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Dass."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, round spot.","A punctuation mark used to indicate the end of a sentence or an abbreviated part of a word; a full stop; a period."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dot"},{"term":"skirt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A separate article of clothing, usually worn by women and girls, that hangs from the waist and covers the lower torso and part of the legs.","A similar part of a dress or robe, etc., that hangs below the waist."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be on or form the border of.","To move around or along the border of; to avoid the center of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skirt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Polka dot","blocks":[{"text":"The polka dot, also written polkadot, and also called spot printed and spot print in the United Kingdom and pois (\"peas\") in France, is a pattern consisting of an array of large filled circles of the same size. Though the dots must be relatively large ones, and must be all the same size in any given print, different styles of polka dot prints may change the size of the dots or the distance between them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Polka_dots.svg/330px-Polka_dots.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polka_dot","wikidata":"Q2429962"},{"title":"Polka","blocks":[{"text":"Polka is a dance style and genre of dance music in 24 originating in nineteenth-century Bohemia, now part of the Czech Republic. Though generally associated with Czech and Central European culture, polka is popular throughout Europe and the Americas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/La_Polka.jpg/330px-La_Polka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polka","wikidata":"Q153071"},{"title":"Skirt","blocks":[{"text":"A skirt is the lower part of a dress or a separate outer garment that covers a person from the waist downwards."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Skirt.jpg/330px-Skirt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skirt","wikidata":"Q2160801"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/2021_SLT_Weert_podium_Alison_Jackson_polkadot_jersey.jpg/500px-2021_SLT_Weert_podium_Alison_Jackson_polkadot_jersey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/2021_SLT_Weert_podium_Alison_Jackson_polkadot_jersey.jpg/500px-2021_SLT_Weert_podium_Alison_Jackson_polkadot_jersey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alison Jackson wears a Queen of the Mountains polkadot cycling jersey","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2021_SLT_Weert_podium_Alison_Jackson_polkadot_jersey.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Bazille_001.jpg/120px-Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Bazille_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Bazille_001.jpg/250px-Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Bazille_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Bazille_001.jpg/120px-Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Bazille_0